  "_comment_theme": "`theme` (the ThemeRef) is REQUIRED on every screen response and lives on the envelope, not in resolvedPreferences -- /screens/event-detail has no preferences block. `themeDocument` is present here because this example models a request whose `knownTheme` did not match (or was omitted); when the client already holds this id@version the server omits it entirely. Its id and version MUST equal `theme`. The document is a verbatim copy of the web client's published light theme (tokens/build/themes/light.json); `version` is content-derived, so regenerate this block whenever the light theme's tokens change. Values typed and platform-neutral: six-digit opaque hex + separate alpha, numeric shadows, font ids from the vendored allowlist. Only the 18 curated semantic roles appear. Calendar fills are derived against THIS document's `surface`: each backgroundColor clears 1.2:1 against it and each foregroundColor clears 4.5:1 against its own fill.",
